# Copy this file to `.env`:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# You do NOT need a key. This dive is a fully offline SIMULATOR of a realtime voice
# session. It models audio frames and per-stage latency deterministically so you
# can see turn-taking, barge-in, and the latency budget without a microphone, a
# speaker, or a provider. There is one provider here: mock.
#
# Production realtime voice uses a speech-to-speech API (OpenAI's Realtime API,
# Google's Gemini Live API) over WebSocket or WebRTC, or a streaming STT->LLM->TTS
# pipeline. See the README. If you wire one up, its API key goes in your OS
# keychain rather than here. See ../docs/SECRETS.md in the series repo:
# https://github.com/alexvervloet/ai-engineering-deep-dive

PROVIDER=mock
